<!--
  Real Kinyarwanda/English localization on Android (2026-08-08+). See bank-mfe/src/i18n's
  own doc comment for the full context. This app previously had NO strings.xml at all in
  the main :app module: every string was hardcoded directly in Kotlin. LoginScreen.kt
  (itunda's own highest-traffic screen) was the first real screen extracted;
  OverviewScreen.kt (the screen every user lands on right after logging in) is the
  second, following the same phased rollout docs/DESIGN_REFERENCES.md Section 19 names.
  Uses Android's own real locale-resource mechanism (values-rw/) for the strings
  themselves, plus its own real printf-style format specifiers (%1$s/%2$d) for the
  handful that carry a dynamic amount/count: Android's native equivalent of the
  {{placeholder}} interpolation added to bank-mfe's own i18n for the same reason.
  Correction: the in-app switcher is NOT AppCompatDelegate.setApplicationLocales, despite
  an earlier version of this comment saying so. See LoginScreen.kt's own doc comment
  for why that API silently doesn't work here (MainActivity extends FragmentActivity, not
  AppCompatActivity) and what replaced it.
-->
